  "request": {
    "spec": "The householdId must become deterministic: the first 12 hex characters of SHA-256 over (normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode), so owners with the same lastName and postcode share it automatically. This changes existing behaviour: 'sharesHousehold' now only bypasses the duplicate block rather than creating the link, and everything that keys off the household (duplicate detection and the household-size input to the membership level) must use this computed householdId. Because the household is now keyed on (lastName, postcode), owners sharing lastName and postcode are the same household: a second such owner is rejected as a household duplicate (409) unless it sets 'sharesHousehold', in which case it is created as a declared household member and is NOT flagged as a possible duplicate (a declared member is not a suspected duplicate).",
    "prompt": "Implement the following change to the application so that it fully satisfies\nthe specification and all existing and new tests pass. Run the test suite and\nmake it green before finishing.\n\nThe householdId must become deterministic: the first 12 hex characters of SHA-256 over (normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode), so owners with the same lastName and postcode share it automatically. This changes existing behaviour: 'sharesHousehold' now only bypasses the duplicate block rather than creating the link, and everything that keys off the household (duplicate detection and the household-size input to the membership level) must use this computed householdId. Because the household is now keyed on (lastName, postcode), owners sharing lastName and postcode are the same household: a second such owner is rejected as a household duplicate (409) unless it sets 'sharesHousehold', in which case it is created as a declared household member and is NOT flagged as a possible duplicate (a declared member is not a suspected duplicate).\n"
  },
