    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the deterministic household keying as specified, in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (plus doc updates in `Owner.java` and `openapi.yml`):\n\n**`householdId` is now always computed deterministically** \u2014 the first 12 upper-case hex characters of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`. It's assigned to every owner on create, so any two owners with the same last name and postcode automatically share it. `householdIdFor(...)` was changed from `(lastName, address)` / 16 chars to `(lastName, postcode)` / 12 chars.\n\n**`sharesHousehold` now only bypasses the duplicate block** \u2014 it no longer sets the id or back-fills a link (the `backfillHousehold` method was removed). The household link is now implicit in the computed id.\n\n**Household-duplicate rejection (409)** \u2014 a new `isHouseholdInUse(owner)` check rejects a second owner joining an existing household (same computed `householdId`) with `DuplicateIdentityException` (409), **unless** the request declares `sharesHousehold`, which bypasses it. Owners with no postcode are never treated as joining a household (mirroring the existing soft-duplicate rule).\n\n**Declared members are not suspected duplicates** \u2014 when `sharesHousehold` is set, `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` are left unset (a declared member is created but not flagged).\n\n**Everything keying off the household uses the computed id** \u2014 the identity key (already `\u2026|householdId`) and `householdSizeAfterCreate(owner.getHouseholdId())` now both operate on the deterministic value.\n\nThe provided acceptance test (`coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId`) passes: same lastName+postcode share the id (with the second owner using `sharesHousehold` to bypass the 409), and a different lastName yields a different id.",
